In order to incorporate the concept of electromagnetic field-controlled quantum state of an electron into the PHP code, you will need to define the Hamiltonian matrix that describes the interaction between the electron and the electromagnetic field. The Hamiltonian matrix can be expressed as H = -μ·B, where μ is the magnetic moment of the electron and B is the magnetic field vector.
To obtain the resulting electron state, you will need to use the time-dependent Schrödinger equation, which can be solved numerically using matrix exponentiation. The resulting state can then be obtained by multiplying the initial state with the time evolution operator.
Here's an example PHP code using NumPy library to implement the above:
<?php
    // Import NumPy library
    require_once('numpy/numpy.php');
    // Define initial state of electron as a matrix
    $initial_state = np_matrix([[1], [0]]);
    // Define Hamiltonian matrix
    $mu = 1;
    $B = np_array([1, 0, 0]);
    $H = np_matrix([[-$mu*$B[2], $mu*$B[1]], [$mu*$B[1], $mu*$B[2]]]);
    // Define time evolution operator
    $t = 0.1;
    $U = np_exp(np_multiply(-1i*$H*$t));
    // Apply time evolution operator to initial state
    $resulting_state = np_dot($U, $initial_state);
    // Print resulting state
    echo $resulting_state;
    // Handle any errors and optimize performance
    // ...
?>
