How can I calculate the number of weekdays between two dates in Swift, taking into account a list of holidays? For example, if my project starts on April 16th and ends on May 21st, and there are holidays on May 1st, May 13th, and May 14th, how many weekdays are there for the team to work on the project?
Here is an array of the holiday dates:
let holidays = ["2022-05-01", "2022-05-13", "2022-05-14"]
And here is the Swift code I currently have for calculating the number of weekdays:
func weekdaysBetween(start: Date, end: Date) -> Int {
    let calendar = Calendar.current
    var weekdays = 0
    var currentDate = start
    while currentDate <= end {
        let weekday = calendar.component(.weekday, from: currentDate)
        if weekday != 1 && weekday != 7 { // Exclude Sunday and Saturday
            weekdays += 1
        }
        currentDate = calendar.date(byAdding: .day, value: 1, to: currentDate)!
    }
    return weekdays
}
How can I modify this code to take into account the list of holidays and exclude them from the count of weekdays?

output:
To modify the code to take into account the list of holidays and exclude them from the count of weekdays, you can add an additional check inside the while loop to exclude the dates that match the holiday dates in the holidays array. Here is the modified code:
```
func weekdaysBetween(start: Date, end: Date, holidays: [String]) -> Int {
    let calendar = Calendar.current
    var weekdays = 0
    var currentDate = start
    while currentDate <= end {
        let weekday = calendar.component(.weekday, from: currentDate)
        if weekday != 1 && weekday != 7 { // Exclude Sunday and Saturday
            let dateString = DateFormatter.localizedString(from: currentDate, dateStyle: .short, timeStyle: .none)
            if !holidays.contains(dateString) { // Exclude holidays
                weekdays += 1
            }
        }
        currentDate = calendar.date(byAdding: .day, value: 1, to: currentDate)!
    }
    return weekdays
}
```
This modified function takes in an additional parameter `holidays` which is an array of holiday dates as strings. Inside the while loop, it converts the current date to a string in the same format as the holiday dates and checks if it exists in the holidays array. If it does, it skips counting that date as a weekday.

